1
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:08,484
The MoU trap. Episode 7. Before you sign

2
00:00:10,984 --> 00:00:13,160
Minister Kerbu: Before we sign anything: who has reviewed it?

3
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:16,980
Enilec Mok: Finance has. Any support is sized to our fiscal space.

4
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:20,203
Paul Ahmak: The utility has. We can pay for what we buy.

5
00:00:20,503 --> 00:00:24,257
Belpau: It is in the least-cost plan, with milestones and a sunset date.

6
00:00:24,557 --> 00:00:26,008
Tidianie Eugom: Then we can lend against it.

7
00:00:26,308 --> 00:00:27,865
Minister Kerbu: Then we sign, and we publish it.

8
00:00:29,615 --> 00:00:32,772
Red team. What turns an MoU into a trap?

9
00:00:33,572 --> 00:00:36,602
It is signed before either test is applied.

10
00:00:37,152 --> 00:00:39,989
It costs its signatories almost nothing.

11
00:00:40,539 --> 00:00:43,632
And the risk bearers are absent when it is signed.

12
00:00:44,182 --> 00:00:48,406
Bring the risk bearers, and their tests, to the start of the process.

13
00:00:51,256 --> 00:00:55,245
Before any power MoU is signed, ask five questions.

14
00:00:55,845 --> 00:00:59,515
One. Is it in the least-cost plan, or tested against it?

15
00:01:00,315 --> 00:01:06,672
Two. Does it carry milestones, a sunset date and, where appropriate, a development security?

16
00:01:07,472 --> 00:01:11,397
Three. Have the utility and the ministry of finance reviewed it?

17
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:16,912
Four. Which layer could block it: sponsor, process, system, or fiscal?

18
00:01:17,712 --> 00:01:20,464
Five. Will it be published in the register?

19
00:01:21,264 --> 00:01:23,525
If not, it is not ready to sign.

20
00:01:26,675 --> 00:01:29,704
An MoU costs almost nothing to sign.

21
00:01:30,604 --> 00:01:32,951
It can cost a great deal later.

22
00:01:34,051 --> 00:01:37,358
Bring the risk bearers, and their tests, to the start.

23
00:01:48,958 --> 00:01:55,422
Thank you for watching the series. Find the full module and the role briefings on Courant Continental.
